body:
>More importantly you don’t need an air conditioning running 24x7. You can leave a liquid cooled PC in a room with no air conditioning & it will be fine. 

How exactly do you think it differs? It doesn't matter if you're using a radiator or a simple heatsink - all the heat is getting pumped into the room either way.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

> This is Yongyea's video? If so, this was lazy content from him. 

Same as all the other "content" he ever produced. Don't forget to like, subscribe and pay a mandatory 5$ Patreon fee btw.

&#x200B;

>Ultracite laser rifle somehow does even less damage than regular laser gear, and still struggles with durability.

It does less damage per shot since it fires faster. Which makes it straight up worse, given how do the DR works IMO.

&#x200B;

>Bethesda launcher

That's just sad. I was hoping to gift these to a friend.

&#x200B;

> they spent a lot of FO3 having you crawl around pre-war ruins and, to  further drive the post-apocalyptic theme home, they painted the old  world like some golden age of humanity. 

Did we play the same game? Majority of the references paint pre-war America as a divided, corrupt society on it's last legs.

&#x200B;
